 checks due together are made once. 256 checks are kept per key.
 
+**Canaries mined before they are due (SOV-012).** When one of a canary's txs confirms (C or C′,
+D, Q), the sidecar posts `POST /sovereignty/canary/resolved` `{"txid": <the canary's txid>,
+"confirmed": <the tx that confirmed>, "height", "time": <block header time>}`. Checks of jobs
+Prime first saw after that block no longer judge the canary: once C′ is mined an honest node's
+template cannot hold C. A canary a block settles before its first due check is therefore not due
+(neither hit nor miss) instead of an honest miss; on 600 s blocks that was ≈ 2% of canaries. A
+proxy's canaries that stay in the mempool are judged as before. The reply says `known: false` for
+a txid primed no longer holds (evicted, or placed before a restart).
+
+**Node addresses for the sidecar (SOV-012).** `GET /sovereignty/nodes` returns what
+`sovereignty-nodes.json` holds, `{G: {"node", "at_height", "updated"}}` for the keys
+`Engine::node_of` answers (active, with a node; superseded, revoked and refused keys are absent).
+The sidecar reads it (`nodes_source = "prime"`), so the file stays 0600 to primed's user.
